   "subject": "Re: Location shinyapps.io servers",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The <a href=\"http://docs.rstudio.com/shinyapps.io/security-and-compliance.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.rstudio.com/shinyapps.io/security-and-compliance.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792359758482000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2s1AbZFRSGexc6aN1qZo0g\">Security and Compliance</a> documentation and <a href=\"https://www.rstudio.com/about/rstudio-and-the-gdpr-what-you-need-to-know/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rstudio.com/about/rstudio-and-the-gdpr-what-you-need-to-know/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792359758482000&amp;usg=AOvVaw30pJNV857Sfp1Qtjw4qEQ1\">GDPR statements</a> are probably what you are looking for.<div><br></div><div>Short answer is that the services is hosted in AWS us-east-1 region and it is not possible to choose the location of servers.</div><div><br></div><div>You might consider looking into one of our on-premise productions <a href=\"https://www.rstudio.com/products/connect/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rstudio.com/products/connect/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792359758482000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1np8SzEMXcYcfi9vzXkBPl\">Connect</a> or <a href=\"https://www.rstudio.com/products/shiny-server-pro/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rstudio.com/products/shiny-server-pro/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792359758482000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0lqO_CvRkxCGKjCIhQ-MO-\">Shiny Server Pro</a>.</div></div>"
